course: dictionary
lesson: 13885
title: Knuckles: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Knuckles can be the joints in your fingers, joints of meat, or part of a phrase. The context tells you which meaning is right. «She knocked on the door with her knuckles.» You knock with your fingers, so knuckles means the finger joints.
explain: «The butcher cut the lamb into knuckles for the roast.» The clues are the butcher, the lamb and the roast, so knuckles means joints of meat. Always ask: what does the sentence show? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Some words sit inside phrases, and the meaning changes. «Tom had to knuckle down to finish his project.» Knuckle down does not mean hitting with your fingers. The clue is finish his project, so it means start working hard.
fact: Knuckles are the joints in your fingers, where they join your hand.
fact: «Knuckles» can also mean joints of meat from an animal's leg.
fact: «Knuckle down» means to start working hard.
fact: «Knuckle under» means to give in.
fact: «Rap on the knuckles» means a telling-off.
exercise: «She knocked on the door with her knuckles.» What are knuckles here? | *Joints in your fingers | Hard lumps of snow | Joints of meat | Pockets in a coat
exercise: «The cold made her knuckles dry and cracked.» Where are the knuckles? | In the ear | On the back of the neck | *On the hand, where the fingers join it | On the knee
exercise: «Tom had to knuckle down to finish his project.» What does knuckle down mean? | *Start working hard | Give up and go home | Hit the table with a fist | Sleep for a long time
test: «The butcher cut the lamb into knuckles for the roast.» What does knuckles mean here? | Small bones in the ear | Knots in a rope | *Joints of meat from an animal's leg | Joints in your fingers
test: «The team refused to knuckle under, even when they were losing.» What does knuckle under mean? | Laugh loudly | Start a new game | Work harder than ever | *Give in
exam: «The teacher gave him a rap on the knuckles for being late.» What does rap on the knuckles mean? | A pat on the hand for a good job | A loud knock on the door | *A telling-off | A cold, wet day
